 "text": "Hey, good to have you back. Are you okay? Sure. It' a color made by combining just a small amount of one color with white from other brush. It evens out the intensity per spot make the colors smoother. In painting, it gives smooth gradient effect. It's particularly useful for those that lack the skills to mix smooth gradients themselves. You could, but it might look too thin. Shadows at eye level need to have some strength. You can use regular black paint and still save bit of pocket by complementing it with a white base. Just a few drops at a maximum.",
